sudotty: px119's probe, sudo's record made on a pseudo-terminal
T1 a pty: /dev/pts/0
T2 the first sudo in session A: asked, the password typed, ran as uid 0
T3 the record it left: tty 34816 sid <the leader's pid> start <the leader's start time> time <ms>
P9 a second sudo in the same session, inside the timeout: not asked, ran as uid 0
T4 session A ended: its leader exited 0
T5 the pair closed and a new one opened: /dev/pts/0, the same number
T6 the stub (PAX never reuses a pid): session A's record given session B's leader's pid, 1 line(s); B's leader started later than A's
P8 a new session on the same pty number, its leader with the earlier leader's pid: asked, the password typed, ran as uid 0
T7 session B ended: its leader exited 0
done
